  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I couldn't find an archived ticket that clearly reports this exact problem. The error is only visible in your screenshot and bug report ZIP, so I couldn't match it to a specific past ticket. The archive does have several similar Command Palette startup failures, and each has a different cause. Check which one applies to you. 1) A crash on launch with v0.99.0 was fixed in v0.99.1 (PowerToys#47453). You are on v0.100.2, so this is probably not your case. 2) Command Palette is installed as a separate MSIX package, and a Windows policy that blocks sideloading can stop it installing (PowerToys#39695). If your PC is managed, or the error mentions sideloading, a policy or deployment failure, check Group Policy for 'Allow all trusted apps to install', 'Allow Sideloading of Apps' and the App Installer policies. Then install the MSIX in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\\\PowerToys\\\\WinUI3Apps\\\\CmdPal manually. 3) Another report of a launch-time crash on v0.99.0 is PowerToys#47249. To get help, please copy the exact error text from the dialog. Also check the logs in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\\\Microsoft\\\\PowerToys\\\\CmdPal\\\\Logs, and include your Windows version and whether the PC is managed by an organization.\"}",
